meta {
  name: 01_ResourceDelegationLifecycle
  seq: 1
}

docs {
  Scenario: A service owner delegates a right on its own resource and revokes it again

    Given the service owner has no delegation of the resource between the two persons
    When the service owner looks up the rights it can delegate on the resource
    And the service owner delegates the read right from the grantor to the recipient
    Then the recipient's authorized parties show the grantor with the resource
    And delegating the same right again returns the same delegation
    When the service owner revokes the delegation
    Then the recipient's authorized parties no longer show the grantor with the resource
    And revoking again is a no-op

  The service owner acts as digdir, which owns the resource. It never needs a relation
  between the two persons in advance: the delegation creates the rettighetshaver
  assignment, and the revoke removes it again because the service owner created it.
}
